# Rheo Quickstart

```elixir
Mix.install(
  [
    # From this repo: prefer the path dep. From HexDocs / standalone Livebook:
    {:rheo, "~> 0.11.0"},
    # {:rheo, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")},
    {:kino, "~> 0.14"}
  ],
  config: [
    rheo: [
      start_on_application: false,
      # Frozen clock lets later notebooks advance time; here it just pins timestamps.
      clock: Rheo.Clock.Frozen,
      default_lease_ms: 5_000,
      default_max_attempts: 3
    ]
  ]
)
```

## Intro

This notebook is the shortest path from “empty BEAM” to a working consumer.
You will:

1. Start Rheo on **ETS** (no Docker, no database)
2. Create a stream and publish a few events
3. Claim work with a **lease**, then **ACK**
4. Run an idiomatic `Rheo.Consumer`

When you finish, continue with [Concepts](concepts.livemd) for fencing, search,
and replay — or jump to [Pipelines](pipelines.livemd) / [Backends](backends.livemd).

<!-- livebook:{"break_markdown":true} -->

### Before you evaluate

1. Open `notebooks/quickstart.livemd` from the repo so the path dependency works
2. Run cells in order — later cells assume earlier bindings (`stream`, etc.)
3. No Docker required

Sibling notebooks: [Concepts](concepts.livemd) · [Pipelines](pipelines.livemd) ·
[Backends](backends.livemd) · [Index](rheo_demo.livemd)

